{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UnVpxZvrPmE7YYbhaHN5rJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1289:Input.THIRDPERSON = {\n1005:- `suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)` †: one step: seen is E.sees' result (or true / false), target the body seen. Returns the state\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest, its head) that the observer's eyes see past every top of o.map, times the target's own exposure (default 1) and .6 when it crouches (it also shows lower). o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye }\n1294:- `walkbox.sees(a, b)` †: can one walk straight from a to b? (it crosses no edge, and its middle is inside)\n1455:- `grid.sees(a, b)`: can a see b: no opaque cell on the line between them (the ends themselves may be)\n963:- `new E.Mover(o = {}) → mover`: new E.Mover({ x, y, z, r: 5, ... }): any of its fields, below, as options. An E.Body: it has body.jump, push and the body's fields too\n968:- `mover.update(dt, map, ctl = {}, view)` †: one step. ctl: game.input (needs the actions move, jump, and sprint / crouch if it has them; screen directions turn into ground ones through view, the game's by default) or an intent { move: [dx, dy], sprint, crouch, jumpPressed }\n1464:- `new E.GridMover(o = {}) → gridmover`: new E.GridMover({ cx, cy, speed: 6 (cells a second) })\n1466:- `gridmover.update(dt, grid, want, o = {})`: a step of dt: want ([dx, dy] or null) is kept until it can be taken. o: { blocked(cx, cy): true where it can't go, push(cx, cy, dx, dy): true when what is in the way moved (a crate), keep: true goes on in the same direction (a maze) }. Returns true when it reached a cell this step\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181310__xac1bf5/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0fcdb66e-7b81-4152-a7ad-a6f1924439c0","uuid":"875f7956-37a2-4861-b9c6-45bc504f91bd","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:17:19.836Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1289:Input.THIRDPERSON = {\n1005:- `suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)` †: one step: seen is E.sees' result (or true / false), target the body seen. Returns the state\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest, its head) that the observer's eyes see past every top of o.map, times the target's own exposure (default 1) and .6 when it crouches (it also shows lower). o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye }\n1294:- `walkbox.sees(a, b)` †: can one walk straight from a to b? (it crosses no edge, and its middle is inside)\n1455:- `grid.sees(a, b)`: can a see b: no opaque cell on the line between them (the ends themselves may be)\n963:- `new E.Mover(o = {}) → mover`: new E.Mover({ x, y, z, r: 5, ... }): any of its fields, below, as options. An E.Body: it has body.jump, push and the body's fields too\n968:- `mover.update(dt, map, ctl = {}, view)` †: one step. ctl: game.input (needs the actions move, jump, and sprint / crouch if it has them; screen directions turn into ground ones through view, the game's by default) or an intent { move: [dx, dy], sprint, crouch, jumpPressed }\n1464:- `new E.GridMover(o = {}) → gridmover`: new E.GridMover({ cx, cy, speed: 6 (cells a second) })\n1466:- `gridmover.update(dt, grid, want, o = {})`: a step of dt: want ([dx, dy] or null) is kept until it can be taken. o: { blocked(cx, cy): true where it can't go, push(cx, cy, dx, dy): true when what is in the way moved (a crate), keep: true goes on in the same direction (a maze) }. Returns true when it reached a cell this step","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181310__xac1bf5/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UnVpxZvrPmE7YYbhaHN5rJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
