und effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n1543:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1570:- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound\n1089:- `E.PROPS: torch, candle, candelabra, chandelier, brazier, window, banner, pillar, statue, crate, barrel, chest, pot, sign, fence, lamp, door, tree, pine, bush, flowers, grass, rock, crystal, bones, skull, vines, cobweb, lantern, streetlamp, awning, hydrant, trashcan, firedrum, sandbags, cactus, palm, mushroom` †: the names of the built-in props for r.prop(name, x, y, z, opts) and E.prop(name, opts)\n1157:- `E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, o = {})`: window frame: ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg, border, shadow, gradient }) bg: one color (drawn as a soft top-to-bottom gradient, like Final Fantasy windows) or [top, bottom] colors. gradient: false for a flat fill.\n1543:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1571:- `rhythm.windows` †: { perfect, great, good } in ms either side of a note\n== car\nkenney-tiny-battle:tile-0006       sprite    166 tok  grey rounded car, white windshield glint, small wheels  [vehicle prop battle]\nkenney-tiny-battle:tile-0024       sprite    161 tok  grey rounded car, narrow glint, variant  [vehicle prop battle]\ncart                               shape     105 tok  hand cart, two wheels, shafts forward  [vehicle farm]\nkaykit-halloween-bits:pumpkin-yellow-jackolantern shape     527 tok  golden yellow pumpkin, faint carved face, short stem  [decoration pumpkin halloween]\n== dumpster\nno match for \"dumpster