isImage\\\":false,\\\"noOutputExpected\\\":false,\\\"bashEditDiff\\\":{\\\"files\\\":[{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181310__xac1bf5/work/WireMeUp-TheWire-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181310.html\\\",\\\"hunks\\\":[{\\\"oldStart\\\":17064,\\\"oldLines\\\":10,\\\"newStart\\\":17064,\\\"newLines\\\":10,\\\"lines\\\":[\\\"     ['Usage', 'unknown']\\\",\\\"   ] },\\\",\\\"   { title: 'TESTING FEEDBACK', rows: [\\\",\\\"-    ['Issues caught', '9 issues caught by testing.'],\\\",\\\"-    ['Critical', '3 would have been game breaking: the camera not following during the briefing (a blank-looking start), a null scene argument that crashed the hub start, and the attract demo ending on the first input it generated itself.'],\\\",\\\"-    ['Most helpful', 'Screenshots of the corner after skipping the briefing with a state dump beside them: they showed layout, readability and AI state at once.'],\\\",\\\"-    ['Least helpful', 'Full-length waits for timed events (the lieutenant\\\\\\\\'s pickup) in a real-time browser; reading the state handle was faster.']\\\",\\\"+    ['Issues caught', '12: the camera not following during the first briefing, center lines drawn as yellow squares, unreadable heat badges, a missing middle-dot glyph, the case board overflowing a 240-pixel screen, the minimize prompt naming Escape (which pauses), a crash pinning a photo, fiends stuck behind buildings, the player car missing its body at the pier, the heat panel under the touch menu button, the wall clock over the room title, and a syntax error from a bad text edit.'],\\\",\\\"+    ['Critical', '3 were game breaking: the crash when pinning a photo (chapter 3 could not be finished), fiends stuck on buildings (the corner could stall), and the syntax error (a blank page).'],\\\",\\\"+    ['Most helpful', 'Scripted playthroughs that pressed through dialogs like a player and read the game state after each step: they found the board crash and the s