aude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"model\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"usage\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"unknown\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"+  },\\\",\\\"+  \\\\\\\"testingFeedback\\\\\\\": [\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"12 issues: the camera not following during the first briefing, center lines drawn as yellow squares, unreadable heat badges, a missing middle-dot glyph, the case board overflowing a 240-pixel screen, the minimize prompt naming Escape (which pauses), a crash when pinning a photo, fiends stuck behind buildings, the player car missing its body at the pier, the heat panel under the touch menu button, the wall clock over the room title, and a syntax error from a bad text edit.\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"3 were game breaking: the crash when pinning a photo (chapter 3 could not be finished), fiends stuck on buildings (the corner could stall), and the syntax error (a blank page).\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"Scripted playthroughs that pressed through dialogs like a player and read the game state after each step; they found the board crash and the stuck fiends.\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"Waiting in real time for timed events in the browser; reading the state handle told me the same thing faster.\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"+  ],\\\",\\\"+  \\\\\\\"engineFeedback\\\\\\\": [\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"Sight, suspicion and sight cones (E.sees, E.Suspicion, r.sightCone) work together out of the box, and dialogs with live portraits made the cast feel real for free.\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"I guessed that a Mover takes world directions from an intent object (it does) and that the pixel font had PlayStation symbols (it does not, so I drew the glyphs myself). I also guessed wrong that E.Dialog's voice is fixed per box; it is read per letter, which let me build the gibberish voices.\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"The camera lens and photo-evidence system: a reticle on the ground, framing, range and line-of-sight checks for each moment worth a picture, and polaroids made from rig portraits.\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"Finding which options wall types and props accept (windows, doors, halos, cones) without reading the source: the options are spread across the card, the index and the guide.\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"The overlapping documentation (card, index, guide, kit headers); one searchable reference with an example per option would be enough.\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"Add PlayStation and Xbox button glyphs to the pixel font, so input.label() can be printed directly in prompts.\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"+  ],\\\",\\\"+  \\\\\\\"promptFeedback\\\\\\\": [\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"The freedom to choose the genre: The Wire is not an action show, and a surveillance game fits it far better than a shooter would.\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"The file name pattern [GameTitle-SOURCE-...] leaves word separators open, and multiplayer 'for the game on its own' could mean local or online play.\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"Fitting every requirement (attract mode, hub, controller-first UI, glyph families, touch notice, four chapters) into one session while keeping the tone right.\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"A real DualSense on a TV at ten feet, to judge prompt size and readability where it matters.\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"+  ],\\\",\\\"+  \\\\\\\"aiHub\\\\\\\": {\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"WIRE ME UP\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"tagline\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"a surveillance story of West Baltimore\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Sit on a West Baltimore corner with a long lens, photograph the hand-to-hands without getting made, crack the crew's pager code, work the wire by the rules, and build the case up to a man nobody has ever photographed.\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Game\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"genre\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Stealth\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The Wire\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"series\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"players\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"1–2\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"controls\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"WASD or stick to move, right mouse or L2 to raise the camera, click or R2 to photograph, C or Circle to crouch, E or Cross to interact\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+    \\\\\\\"tags\\\\\\\": [\\\",\\\"+      \\\\\\\"stealth\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+      \\\\\\\"story\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+      \\\\\\\"top-down\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+      \\\\\\\"pixel art\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+      \\\\\\\"co-op\\\\\\\",\\\",\\\"+      \\\\\\\"crime\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"+    ]\\\",\\\"+  }\\\",\\\"+}\\\"]}],\\\"created\\\":true},{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181325__xe8b2f0/agent.out\\\",\\\"hunks\\\":[{\\\"oldStart\\\":794,\\\"oldLines\\\":3,\\\"newStart\\\":794,\\\"newLines\\\":4,\\\"lines\\\":[\\\" {\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"tool_progress\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"tool_use_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"toolu_01TY6q3gbRrwcjRKVo1rYtHS-heartbeat-0\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"tool_name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Bash\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"toolu_01TY6q3gbRrwcjRKVo1rYtHS\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"elapsed_time_seconds\\\\\\\":30,\\\\\\\"heartbeat\\\\\\\":true,\\\\\\\"session_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"4180323d-f450-4e8c-b0bc-56f3660fbb67\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"uuid\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"b2ecfd3a-b98b-4180-a83f-3d3bb311d3a7\\\\\\\"}\\\",\\\" {\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"tool_progress\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"tool_use_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"toolu_01TY6q3gbRrwcjRKVo1rYtHS-heartbeat-1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"tool_name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Bash\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"toolu_01TY6q3gbRrwcjRKVo1rYtHS\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"elapsed_time_seconds\\\\\\\":60,\\\\\\\"heartbeat\\\\\\\":true,\\\\\\\"session_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"4180323d-f450-4e8c-b0bc-56f3660fbb67\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"uuid\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"75990be9-4707-43f7-9e54-0081aa77eeca\\\\\\\"}\\\",\\\" {\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"system\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"subtype\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"task_notification\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"task_id\\\\\\\